Yes, as is pointed out in the release notes, there is a memory leak
in the X server. It is related to the DPS module in the server.

Unfortunatly, there is not a fix available for this problem. This
problem will be fixed with the introduction of DPS level 2. If you 
are noticing problems with the X servers growth, then the release notes 
suggest that you add the '-terminate' option to the servers line
in /usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xserves. This will cause the server to recyle
(exit & be restarted by xdm) rather than reset at the end of a session.

If you don't use DPS (and want to free up more memory) you can also
comment out the DPS line in the file /usr/lib/X11/Xserver.conf. This
will keep the extension from being loaded.

/Dave


