We had some major performance problems on our DEC 3000/400 under OSF1
v. 1.2 with some FORTRAN codes in particular.  They were running slower
than a 486/66 PC in 32 bit mode.  We found that DEC has a libm.a that
rids us of the problem.  This libm.a will be in the v. 1.3 release (we
haven't got ours yet), but we got a copy from DEC and put it on our
machine.  The performance increased SIGNIFICANTLY for these codes when
we used the -non_shared flag on the compile line (I think you need this
or it will use the junky shared version of libm.a instead of compiling
the whole thing in out of the new, fixed libm.a).  It had no significant
effect on some other codes which must not be using some math routines.
