 Attached you'll find the summary on the MAC <=> OSF/1 ftp problem from the
alpha-osf-manager
 mailing list 

[...] forwards/headers deleted 

It turns out that the criteria of RFC 1122 was turned on only for ftp
services under tcp/ip in OSF/1 V1.2.

The guess was that the Macintosh version of tcp/ip (V1.1.1) did not know
how to deal with this.

Suggested solution:

create a file......

/etc/iptos

ftp-control tcp 0x0
ftp-data tcp 0x0

save it (those are zeros)

reboot

FTP then works from the Macintosh.

This file turns off RFC 1122 somehow.

There is a manual page for iptos by the way.

