|>Are the compilers simply faster in V1.3 or do they produce better
|>code?
|>
|>I.e. should we recompile things to get better performance?
|>
if you compiled non_shared and use exp() or sqrt() alot, recompile, for sure.
if you are using shared libraries(the default) and use exp and sqrt alot, the 
math library fixes should be picked up, so it isn't really necessary.

there are some compiler improvements that might cause you to get better
performance, but mileage varies radically from program to program.  if, for
some reason recompiling is a big hassle for you, it may not be worth it.

