Firstly, this is unofficial.  I'm not a member of the CMU Common Lisp
Group.  Actually, there is no longer a CMU Common Lisp group, it's now
the Igor project.  However, I do work for the same project leader and
with many of the group members. Scott's latest hopes seem to be to have
CMU Common Lisp ported to the Alpha in the next two or three months.  We
only have one Alpha to work with, and the Alpha is inherently wierd, so
it'll take a little time to get running. 

Another thing to point out:  CMUCL releases in the future are liable to
be limited.  DARPA has ceased to fund the CMUCL group and it's members
are now working on a high quality Dylan environment called Igor.  The
main point in doing the DEC OSF/1 port is to have a platform to work
from on that project. 

-Matt 
 


