For those familiar with it, an OSF/1 version of Monitor is
available on gatekeeper.dec.com.  For those not familiar
with it, Monitor is a Curses based performance monitoring
tool.  It collects much of the information available from
iostat, vmstat and netstat in one place.

It can be run interactively, using a user selected update
time, the default based on terminal speed.  For many data
fields more information is collected than can be easily 
displayed on a 24 line terminal.  To allow displaying all
this information it is possible to select a data field and
display the extended information.  In other cases, usually
disks, not all the information will fit on the display.  By
selecting these fields more of the devices can be displayed.
When run on terminal emulators that can send the SIGWINCH
signal, Monitor will resize the display for the new screen
size.

It can also be run non-interactively to save the data to a
file for later replaying or analysis.  Example programs are
included in the distribution for reading the data files.
Documentation and manual pages are also included.

Some of the operating system changes from ULTRIX made keeping
the same data format hard enough that I didn't bother.  The 
distribution includes the same suite of tools and filters as 
the ULTRIX version.

The "proc" and "pid" data options aren't supported, but I've
added some simple swap space utilization, and namei and buffer
cache hit rate stats to the main screen.  Nearly all the data
is collected using the table(2) system call.

The compressed archive is on:

	gatekeeper.dec.com:/pub/DEC/monitor.alpha.Z

					Enjoy


