Wrong

> Will some dec people please enlighten me with correct info.  

CHARACTER            1 Byte
LOGICAL              4 Bytes (=LOGICAL*4)
INTEGER              4 Bytes (=INTEGER*4)
REAL                 4 Bytes (=REAL*4)
DOUBLE PRECISION     8 Bytes (=REAL*8)
COMPLEX              8 Bytes (=COMPLEX*8)
DOUBLE COMPLEX      16 Bytes (=COMPLEX*16)

You can modify the defaults for REAL and INTEGER with the compiler switches
/REAL_SIZE={32,64} and /INTEGER_SIZE={16,32,64}

> What about float and double in dec cc/cxx?

char                 1 Byte
short int            2 Bytes
int                  4 Bytes
long int             4 Bytes
float                4 Bytes
double               8 Bytes
long double          8 Bytes

Martin

