(~{B@TFI=~}Luke Y. Lu) writes:
|>I thought double precision in dec f77 on alpha is real*16 and that real is
|>real*8 since alpha is 64-bit machine.  Will some dec people please
|>enlighten me with correct info.  What about float and double in dec cc/cxx?
|>

Yes, the Alpha AXP architecture is "64 bits", but that means that it has
a 64-bit virtual address space and support for 64-bit integers.  It doesn't
automatically change the size of variables.  Single precision is still four
bytes, double is still 8.  VAX has had REAL*16 (H_float) since 1980 - the
initial lack of a 16-byte floating datatype on AXP has been a concern to
a number of users, hence our work to add support for a type of that size.

