Ultrix provides hidden passwords via the auth database under the ENHANCED
security feature. OSF1 has no ENHANCED security feature (something to
watch out for if you are migrating from Ultrix to OSF1 and are using
the auth database, because passwords are non-transferable). OSF1 does
have (or at least the docs imply that it has) what is called the
Security Integration Architecture. It looks like SIA can be used to
implement hidden passwords, 16-byte encrypted passwords, or anything you
want. The doc says that all of the important programs (login, telnetd,
su, ...) use SIA, and it is just a matter of replacing the 
/etc/sia/matrix.conf file with one that describes how to use alternative
getpwent() et al routines. That's where the docs stop.


Does anybody know where an Interface Definition is for SIA describing
how to provide custom routines. Or better yet, is there an SIA product
out there that uses hidden passwords (preferably crypt16() passwords)? Is 
SIA a DEC thing or an OSF thing?


-- 
