There's been some interest in getting gnuplot going on DEC Alpha /
OSF1.  Here's how to do it:

1.  In files plot.c and parse.c, the argument to the signal function
is not prototyped correctly by default.  Alpha compilers define
__alpha, so stick this in along with the others in the ansii
prototypes (the same line as the cray and sgi).

2.  Hack the flags for dec_osf in the makefile as follows:

Add a -ldnet_stub to bith library lines
Change the vfork thing to relect the fact that osf1 HAS vfork
Change the gamma thing to relect the fact that osf1 HAS gamma

Add -Olimit 1000 after where optimisation is specified.

3.  Use c89 if you have it.  If you use cc, turn off optimisation.
The optimiser does not work with gnuplot.


These updates have been communicated to the Gnuplot maintainers.

