I haven't seen V1.3 yet. If the 1.2 release is anything to go by then us lot
here (not sure if it's just this particular place, or the UK in general)
probably won't get to see it for ages yet. We were substantially behind the US
in updates during the beta test stages it seemed - a bit pointless really for
beta testing.

My *personal* views (well, all of this is anyway) are that I prefer OSF/1. The
reasons behind this are pretty much simply because I'd never used a non BSD
derived system before Solaris 2.x, and that attempting to use the BSD
compatibility libraries on Solaris 2.x simply yields problems after problems.
If you're going to use Solaris 2.x then please forget the existance of these
libraries. Although I will admit (grudgingly :-) that I'm starting to get used
