making changes for apparently no reason at all (eg renaming fstab to vfstab,
swapping around arguments on ls, etc). These changes aren't _wrong_, just down
right confusing to start with.

As far as portability issues go, I think we need code that works on both SVR4
and BSD derived systems. Where there are common bits in OSes (eg POSIX) then I
guess we can use such things. But I cannot see one or t'other going down the
drain just yet.

